---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const pageUrl = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site).toString();
const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: 'About CSV Toolbox',
    url: pageUrl,
    description: 'Learn about CSV Toolbox: our mission, technology stack (Astro, Web Workers), privacy-first client-side architecture, and open source development.',
    mainEntity: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'CSV Toolbox',
      url: Astro.site?.toString(),
      logo: new URL('/favicon.svg', Astro.site).toString(),
      sameAs: [
        'https://www.instagram.com/freecsvtoolbox',
        'https://www.pinterest.com/freecsvtoolbox',
        'https://github.com/Dx1100/csv-toolbox'
      ],
      description: 'Free, private, browser-based CSV and tabular data utilities built for analysts, developers, and spreadsheet users.'
    }
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: Astro.site?.toString() },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: pageUrl }
    ]
  }
];
---

<Base
  title="About CSV Toolbox — Mission, Technology & Privacy Architecture"
  description="Learn about CSV Toolbox: our mission, technology stack (Astro, HTML5 Web Workers), 100% client-side privacy architecture, and open source development."
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="container guide">
    <h1>About CSV Toolbox</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      CSV Toolbox is an independent, zero-latency web utility built for data analysts, marketers, software engineers, and spreadsheet users who demand fast, private tabular data processing.
    </p>

    <h2>Our Core Principle: Zero-Upload Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Traditional online converter tools force you to upload your sensitive spreadsheets to remote cloud servers. This exposes confidential financial data, customer PII, and medical records to security breaches, compliance violations (GDPR/HIPAA), and slow upload bottlenecks.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>CSV Toolbox solves this by executing 100% of data processing directly inside your web browser.</strong> Using HTML5 Web Workers, modern stream readers (<code>FileReader</code> API), and client-side memory chunking, your files never leave your device. When you close the browser tab, your data vanishes completely from memory.
    </p>

    <h2>The Technology Stack</h2>
    <p>
      Every tool on CSV Toolbox is engineered for maximum speed, low resource consumption, and reliability:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Astro 5 SSG:</strong> Server-first static HTML compilation ensuring near-instant page load times (LCP &lt; 0.8s) and zero runtime JavaScript bloat.</li>
      <li><strong>HTML5 Web Workers:</strong> Heavy parsing algorithms run on isolated background CPU threads, preventing your browser tab or UI from freezing even on 500MB+ datasets.</li>
      <li><strong>Streaming PapaParse &amp; JSZip:</strong> Battle-tested, memory-optimized open-source libraries for streaming delimiter detection, row chunking, and multi-file archive generation.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare Edge Network:</strong> Hosted globally across Cloudflare's serverless edge with Full Strict SSL encryption and Brotli compression.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Open Source &amp; Community Backed</h2>
    <p>
      We believe data privacy requires transparency. The complete source code for CSV Toolbox is publicly auditable on our <a href="https://github.com/Dx1100/csv-toolbox" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository</a>. You can inspect every line of parser logic to verify that zero external network requests are made with your file data.
    </p>

    <h2>Support &amp; Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      CSV Toolbox is supported by non-intrusive advertising, which keeps every utility 100% free with no signups, no subscriptions, and no file size paywalls. Have a feature request or need a new delimiter tool? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch with us</a> or open an issue on GitHub.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
